                "modelAnswer": "a) Adverse effects of carbamazepine: (1) Dizziness/drowsiness, (2) Hyponatremia, (3) Rash/Stevens-Johnson syndrome, (4) Bone marrow suppression (e.g., agranulocytosis).\n\nb) Strategies to minimize adverse effects: (1) Start with a low dose and titrate slowly to reduce CNS adverse effects, (2) Monitor serum sodium and complete blood counts regularly to detect hyponatremia and bone marrow suppression early."
