                "stem": "a) List four (4) non-motor symptoms of Parkinson’s disease. (4 marks)\n\nb) Explain two (2) mechanisms by which these symptoms arise. (6 marks)",
                "modelAnswer": "a) Non-motor symptoms of Parkinson’s disease include:\n1. Cognitive impairment/dementia\n2. Depression and anxiety\n3. Sleep disturbances (e.g., REM sleep behavior disorder, insomnia)\n4. Autonomic dysfunction (e.g., orthostatic hypotension, constipation, urinary incontinence)\n5. Sensory symptoms (e.g., pain, paresthesia)\n6. Fatigue\n\nb) Mechanisms underlying non-motor symptoms:\n1. **Neurodegeneration beyond dopaminergic neurons**: Parkinson’s disease involves progressive loss of neurons in non-dopaminergic systems (e.g., serotonergic, noradrenergic, cholinergic), contributing to mood disorders, sleep disturbances, and cognitive impairment.\n2. **Alpha-synuclein pathology**: Lewy body accumulation in limbic and cortical regions disrupts neural circuits, leading to cognitive decline, psychiatric symptoms, and autonomic dysfunction.\n3. **Neuroinflammation and oxidative stress**: Chronic neuroinflammation and mitochondrial dysfunction may exacerbate neuronal damage in non-dopaminergic pathways, worsening non-motor symptoms."
