                  "d": "**Long-Term Management**:\n   - **Antiretroviral Therapy (ART)**: Initiate ART within 2 weeks of starting PCP therapy to restore immune function and prevent recurrence.\n     - Recommended regimen: **Tenofovir + emtricitabine + dolutegravir (TDF/FTC/DTG)** or **abacavir + lamivudine + dolutegravir (ABC/3TC/DTG)**.\n   - **Secondary Prophylaxis**:\n     - Continue TMP-SMX 160/800mg PO daily for secondary prophylaxis against PCP.\n     - Consider discontinuing secondary prophylaxis if CD4 count increases to >200 cells/mm³ for >3 months.\n   - **Patient Education**:\n     - Counsel on the importance of adherence to ART and PCP prophylaxis.\n     - Discuss risk reduction strategies (e.g., safe sex, avoiding IV drug use).\n     - Schedule regular follow-up appointments to monitor CD4 count, HIV viral load, and clinical status."
