                "stem": "Define clinical pharmacy and list FIVE key roles of a clinical pharmacist in a hospital setting.",
                "modelAnswer": "Clinical pharmacy is a health science discipline that involves the direct provision of medication-related care to patients to optimize therapeutic outcomes. Key roles of a clinical pharmacist in a hospital setting include:\n1. Medication review and reconciliation to ensure appropriateness and safety.\n2. Identifying and resolving drug-related problems (e.g., interactions, dosing errors).\n3. Providing patient counseling on medication use, adherence, and side effects.\n4. Monitoring for adverse drug reactions (ADRs) and reporting to pharmacovigilance systems.\n5. Participating in antimicrobial stewardship programs to promote rational antibiotic use.\n6. Collaborating with healthcare teams to develop individualized treatment plans.\n7. Educating healthcare professionals and patients on medication safety and efficacy."
