                "stem": "A 40-year-old patient presents to the pharmacy with a prescription for amoxicillin/clavulanate 625 mg three times daily for a suspected urinary tract infection. The patient mentions they are allergic to penicillin. \n\na) What is the MOST likely risk associated with this prescription? (1 mark)\n\nb) What is the MOST appropriate action for the pharmacist to take? (2 marks)\n\nc) If the patient insists on taking the medication despite the allergy, what should the pharmacist do? (2 marks)",
