                "modelAnswer": "Clinical pharmacy is a health science discipline that involves the direct provision of medication-related care to patients to optimize therapeutic outcomes and improve quality of life. Key roles of a clinical pharmacist in a hospital setting include:\n1. Medication therapy management: Reviewing and optimizing medication regimens for efficacy, safety, and cost-effectiveness.\n2. Patient counselling: Educating patients on medication use, side effects, and adherence strategies.\n3. Medication reconciliation: Ensuring accurate transfer of medication information across care transitions.\n4. Adverse drug reaction (ADR) monitoring: Identifying, reporting, and managing ADRs to prevent harm.\n5. Antimicrobial stewardship: Promoting rational antibiotic use to combat antimicrobial resistance."
