                "modelAnswer": "a) Classes of drugs CONTRAINDICATED for acute migraine in a patient with Prinzmetal (variant) angina:\n• ERGOT ALKALOIDS — ergotamine and dihydroergotamine: potent vasoconstrictors (α-adrenergic/5-HT agonism) that can precipitate coronary vasospasm.\n• TRIPTANS (5-HT1B/1D agonists) — e.g., sumatriptan, zolmitriptan: cause coronary vasoconstriction and are contraindicated in ischemic heart disease/Prinzmetal angina.\n\nb) Classes of drugs recommended for migraine PROPHYLAXIS in this patient (with examples):\n1. β-ADRENERGIC BLOCKERS — propranolol (standard first-line migraine prophylactic; use with caution in vasospastic angina — preferred if no resting ischemia).\n2. CALCIUM CHANNEL BLOCKERS — flunarizine or verapamil (useful both for migraine prophylaxis and for treating Prinzmetal angina — a particularly suitable choice here).\n3. TRICYCLIC ANTIDEPRESSANTS — amitriptyline (effective prophylactic; also helps with comorbid depression/anxiety and neuropathic pain)."
