                "stem": "A 45-year-old man with HIV on ART presents with a 2-week history of fever, night sweats, and weight loss. Chest X-ray shows a right upper lobe infiltrate. Sputum microscopy reveals acid-fast bacilli. (a) Identify the most likely pathogen. (1 mark) (b) Outline the recommended treatment regimen. (2 marks) (c) Describe the mechanism of action of rifampicin. (2 marks) (d) State two drug interactions of rifampicin that are relevant to this patient. (2 marks)",
