                "stem": "COVID-19 Pandemic has had a huge Global impact, Central to the fight against Covid-19 is the clinical development of drugs. You have been tasked as a drug Specialist to assist in undertaking research on New Drug Development. Give a description of the four Clinical phases of New Drug Development. (12 Marks)",
                "modelAnswer": "The four clinical phases of new drug development:\n• Phase 1: First administration to humans — small number (20–100) of healthy volunteers (or sometimes patients). Purpose: safety, tolerability, pharmacokinetics (absorption, distribution, metabolism, excretion), maximum tolerated dose and dose-limiting toxicity.\n• Phase 2: Therapeutic exploratory — 100–300 patients with the target disease. Purpose: preliminary evidence of efficacy, dose–response/optimal dose finding, short-term safety and common side effects.\n• Phase 3: Therapeutic confirmatory — large trials (1,000–5,000+ patients), often randomised, controlled, multicentre, sometimes blinded, comparing the drug with placebo and/or standard treatment. Purpose: confirm efficacy, establish the benefit–risk (safety) profile and detect relatively common adverse reactions; data support registration/marketing authorisation.\n• Phase 4: Post-marketing surveillance — after the drug is marketed, in the general population (thousands to millions). Purpose: detect rare, delayed or long-term adverse reactions, drug–drug interactions, special populations (pregnancy, children, elderly), new indications and pharmacovigilance reporting."
